// Title: IE Change Domain Zone
// Sigma ID: 45e112d0-7759-4c2a-aa36-9f8fb79d3393
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-01-22 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1137
// Description: Hides the file extension through modification of the registry
// False positives:
//   - Administrative scripts
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1112/T1112.md#atomic-test-4---add-domain-to-trusted-sites-zone
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/developer/browsers/security-privacy/ie-security-zones-registry-entries
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_change_security_zones.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\ZoneMap\\Domains.*$" and (not((RegistryValueData in~ ("DWORD (0x00000000)", "DWORD (0x00000001)", "(Empty)"))))
